---
layout: layouts/specimen.njk
title: Water specimen — Watered
description: Interactive SPHjs water followed by three CSS water alternatives.
specimenSection: water
bodyClass: page-fluid-study
---

{% from "components/water.njk" import water %}

<header>
  <p class="type-small">Water specimen</p>
  <h1 class="type-display">A little movement.</h1>
  <p class="type-lead">
    Interactive SPHjs water, followed by three CSS alternatives.
    Resize the page and pause each study to compare their surfaces.
  </p>
</header>

<nav class="fluid-study-nav" aria-label="Water studies">
  <a href="#water-simulation-title">SPHjs simulation</a>
  <a href="#water-study-title">CSS alternatives</a>
</nav>

{% include "components/fluid-study.njk" %}

<section class="water-study" aria-labelledby="water-study-title">
  <h2 id="water-study-title" class="type-heading">CSS waves</h2>
  <label class="water-study-control">
    <input type="checkbox" class="water-study-pause" id="pause-water">
    Pause water
  </label>
  <div class="water-scene" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="water-pool"></div>
    <div class="water-surface"></div>
  </div>
  <p class="type-small water-study-caption">
    Decorative motion only; this study does not simulate pouring or accumulated volume.
    Reduced-motion preferences keep the water still.
  </p>
</section>

<p class="type-small">
  Technique reference:
  <a href="https://www.geekboots.com/css/water-wave-animation?tab=code">Geekboots’ CSS water wave animation</a>.
</p>

<section class="water-study water-study--rolling" aria-labelledby="water-rolling-title">
  <h2 id="water-rolling-title" class="type-heading">Rolling water</h2>
  <label class="water-study-control">
    <input type="checkbox" class="water-study-pause" id="pause-water-rolling">
    Pause rolling water
  </label>
  <div class="water-scene water-scene--rolling" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="water-pool"></div>
    <div class="water-surface"></div>
  </div>
  <p class="type-small water-study-caption">
    A full-width pool with deeper shading and a more pronounced rolling surface.
    The water level stays constant; this is decorative motion, not loading progress.
  </p>
</section>

<p class="type-small">
  Technique reference:
  <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OGQTueiKhnU">Online Tutorials’ Liquid Loader Animation Effects</a>.
</p>

<section class="water-study water-study--bubbles" aria-labelledby="water-bubbles-title">
  <h2 id="water-bubbles-title" class="type-heading">Still water, rising bubbles</h2>
  <label class="water-study-control">
    <input type="checkbox" class="water-study-pause" id="pause-water-bubbles">
    Pause bubbles
  </label>
  <div class="water-scene water-scene--bubbles" aria-hidden="true">
    {{ water() }}
  </div>
  <p class="type-small water-study-caption">
    A still, bubble-free water texture with a clean fixed waterline.
    Only the bubbles move, using CSS; reduced motion leaves calm water.
  </p>
</section>
